course: dictionary
lesson: 3845
title: Fossil
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A fossil is the remains or trace of a living thing from long ago, kept in rock. «A fossil is the remains or trace of a living thing from long ago kept in rock.» The clues are long ago and kept in rock, so a fossil is not a living animal. It is what is left behind.
explain: Fossils form when remains are buried in mud, and the mud slowly turns to rock. Scientists dig up fossils and study them to learn how living things have changed over millions of years. «Fossil hunting» means searching the ground for these traces.
explain: Be careful: the word fossil has more than one meaning. «Coal, oil and natural gas are fossil fuels» means fuels made from ancient living things. Joking about «an old fossil» means an old-fashioned person. Use the words around it to choose the right meaning.
fact: A fossil is the remains or trace of a living thing from long ago, kept in rock.
fact: «Fossil fuels» means coal, oil and gas, made from ancient living things over millions of years.
fact: Fossils show how living things have changed over millions of years, and they give evidence about dinosaurs.
fact: Many dinosaur skeletons are casts, copies made from moulds, because real fossil bones are heavy, fragile and rare.
fact: About 250 million years ago the continents were joined in one land called Pangaea, which is why the same fossils are found in Africa and South America.
exercise: «A fossil is the remains or trace of a living thing from long ago kept in rock.» What is a fossil? | A new kind of rock that glows in the dark | *The remains or trace of a living thing from long ago, kept in rock | A tool that builders use to dig | A type of car fuel bought at a petrol station
exercise: «Coal, oil and natural gas are fossil fuels formed over millions of years from ancient plants and animals.» Which of these is a fossil fuel? | *Coal | Rain | Wind | Sunlight
exercise: Grandad laughs and says, «I'm an old fossil!» What does he mean? | *He is old-fashioned, and he is joking | He has turned into rock | He is very rich | He is a real dinosaur bone
test: «Many dinosaur skeletons are casts, copies made from moulds, because real fossil bones are heavy, fragile and rare.» Why are many dinosaur skeletons casts? | Because fossils can talk | Because dinosaurs were made of plastic | Because museums prefer shiny things | *Because real fossil bones are heavy, fragile and rare
test: «About 250 million years ago the continents were joined in one land called Pangaea, which is why the same fossils are found in Africa and South America.» Why are the same fossils found in both places? | Because animals swam across the whole ocean in one day | *Because the continents were once joined together | Because fossils are made in shops | Because both places are very hot
exam: What does «fossil fuels» mean in «Coal, oil and natural gas are fossil fuels formed over millions of years from ancient plants and animals»? | Fuels that will never run out | *Fuels made from ancient living things | Fuels made by the sun this week | Fuels made from plastic bottles
